From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:22:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s5l8960x: Keep the ANS DLL powered

ans_dll, the ANS's NAND interface DLL (the ADT's ANS_DLL clock gate), has
no consumer, so genpd powers it off as unused while the ANS is running.
On an iPad mini 2 (J85) the ANS then took 10 to 30 s per command after
it woke from s2idle, journald's watchdog fired, and at boot the
firmware reported a garbage collection of 70 seconds. Keep it on, as
iOS does whenever the ANS is up. ps_ans is its parent and already stays
on.

With it on, two rounds of s2idle on the J85 came back with the disk
answering at once.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/221#issuecomment-7124272492
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-pmgr.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-pmgr.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-pmgr.dtsi
index 39b408b09..8ac81c7bd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-pmgr.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-pmgr.dtsi
@@ -590,6 +590,12 @@ ps_ans_dll: power-controller@20208 {
 		#reset-cells = <0>;
 		label = "ans_dll";
 		power-domains = <&ps_ans>;
+		/*
+		 * The NAND interface's DLL (ADT clock gate ANS_DLL). Nothing
+		 * in Linux claims it, and with it off the ANS slows to
+		 * seconds per command after it wakes from sleep.
+		 */
+		apple,always-on;
 	};
 
 	ps_gfx: power-controller@20218 {
